statement:
Let P, m ∈ ℕ, let G : ℝ^m → ℝ^P be of class C¹ (ContDiff ℝ 1 G; ℝ^k = Euclid k), x ∈ ℝ^m and r ∈ ℝ. Assume:
- G is injective on the closed ball B̄_r(x) = {z : |z − x| ≤ r};
- DG(z) = fderiv ℝ G z is injective for every z in the open ball B_r(x) = {z : |z − x| < r}.
Then N := G(B_r(x)) is an embedded m-dimensional C¹ submanifold of ℝ^P in the sense of the contract (IsEmbeddedSubmanifold 1 m N). That is, every y ∈ N has an open W ∋ y, an open V ⊆ ℝ^m and a map ψ such that:
- ψ is C¹ on V and injective on V;
- ψ(V) = W ∩ N;
- V ∩ ψ⁻¹(K) is compact for every compact K ⊆ W;
- Dψ(z) is injective for every z ∈ V.
If r ≤ 0, then N = ∅ and the statement is vacuous.
